# key-ring (M13a): a key pressed on a part a press focused shows its ring, as :focus-visible comes
# to match an element the keyboard interacts with, and nothing more: no focus event comes of it,
# so the box's keys tip, which React shows on a focus that came from the keyboard (NumberBox's
# onKeyboardFocus), stays away (the run file's M13a carry-over; M9 did it for the plane). k's box
# (330, 452.5, 107 x 32 at 1440 x 900) dragged 50 px: the press focused it, no ring, k 1.00; →
# nudges it to 1.01 and its ring shows, no tip. a's flip (296, 412.5, 24 x 24) clicked: Chromium
# focuses a button on a click, which the port follows (plan call 3 f), no ring; x, a key the flip
# takes no action on, shows its ring. Reset all (358.12, 366.5, 84.88 x 20) clicked hands its focus
# to a's box, no ring; ↑ nudges a to 1.01 and a's ring shows, no tip. WebKit's click focuses no
# button, so there x and ↑ reach no part after the flip's click and Reset all's: judge those
# against Chromium (call 3 f).
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 383 468
wait 16
down
move 433 468 over 160
up
wait 700
shot dragged
key ArrowRight
wait 700
shot box-key
click 308 424
wait 1000
shot flip-clicked
key x
wait 16
shot flip-key
click 400 376
wait 1000
shot reset-clicked
key ArrowUp
wait 700
shot reset-key
